> So a while ago, I thought about trying a "no Magic Resistance" conduct,
> but never got around to it.  Now I'm looking at my chaotic priest
> LittleWhiteMouse on NAO and thinking he's going to be my best shot, so I'm
> gonna do it.

> The biggest threats I see are:
> 1)  L  (solution?  b?oG)

That will almost be required, unless you make copious use of Elbereth.
(That's another conduct that should be tracked, by the way, scribing
Elbereth.)

> 2)  Polymorph ^ (solution?  I've already been wearing a =oPC for most of
> the game due to no MR early)

If you're wearing DSM and aren't polycontrolled, you'll always turn
into a dragon.  If you polymorph again before it wears off, however,
you might break out of your armor, so beware.

> 3)  Nasty spells that do massive damage (solution?  loooots of alchemy?)

Even those spells don't typically do *that* much damage, I believe, if
you're prepared for them.  Having a quest artifact that gives half
spell damage could help there.

> 4)  Priests (they can cast FoD, right?) (solution?  Kill them from far
> away!)

I don't know if they can or not but I don't think so, Priests get
different spells than the more typical magic users.

> 5)  Rodney.  This one doesn't give as easy a solution - he'll have
> chances to get close to me no matter what I do, AFAICanTell.  I'll have to
> hope for very quick kills on him and use "oLifeSaving.

When he teleports in, it's usually at melee range.  Unless you pay very
careful attention to your moves on the way up, it's easy to give him a
free turn which might be all he needs.

> I haven't done any polymorphing objects yet (nor wishing, for that
> matter), and I'm not too keen to break that conduct, but the potential to
> have 5-6 "oLS is very tempting!
>
> Am I missing any big threats?  Any thoughts?

You can survive a touch of death spell from all sources but Death by
hallucinating when it hits.  ("You have an out of body experience.")
It's the only benefit to hallucination of which I'm aware.

Wands of death could be a big problem if a monster gets one before you
get a means of reflection, but until Orcus those are completely random.

The Destroy Armor spell could potentially be very dangerous for you
unless you keep on hand spare equipment, which can quickly load up even
a bag of holding.  At least one type of naga can cast it too
(guardian?).

Then there's Death himself, who, if you end up having to face him,
you'll have to handle very carefully.  You might be able to jump by him
(does the jump spell work on Astral or does it count as teleporting?).
Being very fast might help, but jumping might be better.  It'd be
useful to get some of the priests around there to summon insects.
Conflict could also be a great aid, to make monsters waste turns
attacking and possibly killing each other.  Displacement (also
invisibility?) can also give you that one turn advantage necessary to
scoot by Death.  I suppose walling him off with boulders could work,
although it'd be difficult.

I'll be very interested to hear what your experience is.  In my most
recent ascension, on which I most certainly *did* have magic
resistance, no monster was able to get a finger of death off on me.
There was definitely a luck component to that though, I was always able
to kill the Wizard of Yendor with my own finger of death - which I was
safe from due to the amulet of reflection from Sokoban -- and didn't
have to face Death on the Astral Plane.

If you're going to do without MR anyway, you might as well make the
most of it.  It means you can more reasonably go with a cloak of
displacement, or oilskin to help you out with sea monsters.  It also
means that SDSM is obviously your choice of armor, if you can create
it.

Good luck!

